<a href="https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-szaOQrbcn1M/VxU1s_a3uaI/AAAAAAAABW8/YETrldyPM8wjvcgh84jlKqCPZwO5BCJMgCLcB/s1600/sga.png" imageanchor="1" style="clear: left; float: left; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"><img border="0" height="200" src="https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-szaOQrbcn1M/VxU1s_a3uaI/AAAAAAAABW8/YETrldyPM8wjvcgh84jlKqCPZwO5BCJMgCLcB/s200/sga.png" width="186" /></a></div>
Both pairs of candidates received 30 percent of the student vote, with a total of 3,296 students participating. Elections for the runoff will re-open on Friday, April 15, at 1 p.m. and close on April 19 at 4 p.m. Winners will be announced that day at 6 p.m. Students can vote through&nbsp;<a href="http://www.elections.gatech.edu/">www.elections.gatech.edu/</a>.<span class="&#8221;fullpost&#8221;"></span><br />
<div>
<br /></div>
<div>
To see a list of representatives that have already been decided click <a href="http://www.news.gatech.edu/2016/04/14/race-continues-undergraduate-sga-election-updates">here</a>.</div>
