</h2>
<div class='date'>
<span class='author'>
Posted by
<span class='fn'>Admin</span>
</span>
<span class='clock'>

        On
      
4:30:00 PM
</span>
<span class='comm'>
<a class='comment-link' href='http://georgiatechhts.blogspot.com/2016/04/david-hounshell-talk-at-gt.html#comment-form' onclick=''>0
comments</a>
</span>
</div>
</div>
<style>.fullpost{display:none;}</style>
<div class='entry'>
<div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;">
<a href="https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-rcM20MSNVqo/Vw_9sHLlloI/AAAAAAAABVo/jMu_M-MdA4kC3jQCnfTV42nScB7ma3YfgCLcB/s1600/David%2BHounshell.jpg" imageanchor="1" style="clear: left; float: left; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"><img border="0" height="200" src="https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-rcM20MSNVqo/Vw_9sHLlloI/AAAAAAAABVo/jMu_M-MdA4kC3jQCnfTV42nScB7ma3YfgCLcB/s200/David%2BHounshell.jpg" width="170" /></a></div>
David Hounshell, one of the leading historians of technology and business historians in the U.S., will be speaking at GT on Monday afternoon at 4:00 on the history of R&amp;D. His talk titled "What Led to the Rise of&nbsp;Industrial Research in America, Why Did It Once Flourish, and What Led&nbsp;to Its Decline?" will be held at 4:00 p.m. in the GTMI Auditorium.<div>
<br />There will be a reception in the GTMI Atrium at 3:30 p.m.</div>
